{
    "word": "limekiln",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1777b886-45de-3f3e-9dbe-4cca90aa84b7",
                "word": "limekiln",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "66cabb97-a59e-4923-9edd-ba93334e4ddb",
                        "entry_id": "1777b886-45de-3f3e-9dbe-4cca90aa84b7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "limekilns"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                        "entry_id": "1777b886-45de-3f3e-9dbe-4cca90aa84b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A furnace used to produce lime from limestone."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad2db88a-6c0b-4c3d-987d-3a0462c984ff",
                                "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                                "text": "Thou mightst as well say I love to walk by the Counter-gate, which is as hateful to me as the reek of a lime-kiln."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70934e98-dcc3-425b-8fa2-21b71d7077ac",
                                "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                                "text": "From head to foot I was powdered almost as white with chalk and dust, as if I had come out of a lime-kiln."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2283233a-ed21-4a23-83ff-c6f74a655178",
                                "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                                "text": "He wasn’t comfortable, he said. And he’d got a thirst like a lime kiln. And he’d noticed that there was no water-bottle in the room."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31846a98-ddda-4f77-a60d-1d128bafb7be",
                                "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                                "text": "“I can’t be dead,” he reflected. “I have a villainous headache, and my mouth is like a lime-kiln […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d94c0ac3-35c1-434e-930a-6ef36a6441ce",
                                "sense_id": "a84d0059-3a42-3140-ac21-0a1e92909254",
                                "text": "His body was far from comfortable, for he was not accustomed to squatting or lolling, and the heat of the fire and the heavy flavour of food and ale had made the place like a limekiln."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efb2ad00-990e-3522-9582-b91834b08b13",
                        "entry_id": "1777b886-45de-3f3e-9dbe-4cca90aa84b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A burning sensation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "880d00dc-f054-42ee-b2f0-47b2d63019c9",
                                "sense_id": "efb2ad00-990e-3522-9582-b91834b08b13",
                                "text": "Now, the rotten diseases of the south, the guts-griping, ruptures, catarrhs, loads o’ gravel i’ the back, lethargies, cold palsies, raw eyes, dirt-rotten livers, wheezing lungs, bladders full of imposthume, sciaticas, limekilns i’ the palm, incurable bone-ache, and the rivelled fee-simple of the tetter, take and take again such preposterous discoveries!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
